+## Changed
+
+- `run` now starts pi once through the runners kernel's `run_task` with `PiHarness::from_config`, the executor role, no start retries, zero delays, an empty agent env, the executor config's model and the task timeout. It appends `started`, every harness event, `exited` and, when the result file predates the start, `exit_continued` to `.run/events/<task>.jsonl`.
+- Added the before/after git snapshots (`GitVcs::status` with a SHA-256 of each file's bytes), the changed-path classification (`Deleted`, `Added`, `Modified`), the nearest-`Cargo.toml` `tests`/`benches` folders and Rust's/TypeScript's lock rules. Core's `audit_scope` decides: outside paths append `scope_violation` and die, frozen tests die as `undeclared_test_change`.
+- Added the verdict: a missing result dies as `no_result`, a real `## Blocked` section as `blocked`, then the task's verify and the proposal's verify run through `run_verify` with their config timeouts and kill grace, appending `verify_ran` to the task stream and `change.jsonl`. Red verifies die as `verify_red`/`change_verify_red` with `command:`, `timed_out: true` and `exit_code:` where the delta asks, and the last 2000 bytes of the output.
+- Added the done record: `.run/done/<task>` with a UTC time and newline, a `done` event, `tick_task_checkbox` on `tasks.md`, and the `Task <task> of <folder> done` ending. The lock is released on every path.
+- Added the executable fake pi at `tests/fixtures/fake-pi/run.sh` with the nine outcome modes plus extra modes for timeouts, a long verify output, allowed audit paths and a usage-free hang, and `tests/run_outcomes.rs` proving "Run outcomes", "Dead event", "Lock removed after a run", "Executor exits", "Scope outcomes" and "Done task" plus timeout and marker coverage.
+- `crates/features/run/Cargo.toml` gained `osq-kernel-runners`, `osq-kernel-harnesses` and the workspace's existing `sha2` for the file hashes.
+
+## Deviated
+
+- A failed start is reported with the task-two transitional text, `task <task> of <folder> cannot start yet`, instead of the `crashed` death the "Executor start" requirement gives a failed start. Task two left `run_passing_approval_takes_and_removes_the_lock` in `crates/features/run/tests/run_refusals.rs` asserting that exact line, and that file is outside this task's scope and the task sets no `tests.modify`, so the watcher forbids changing it. A pi that spawns and exits non-zero still dies as `crashed`, and a timeout as `timeout`.
+- File hashing uses the workspace's `sha2` instead of hand-written arithmetic; the delta only asks for a hash.
+
+## Missing context
+
+- The task says it replaces the `cannot start yet` line task two wrote, but it does not put `crates/features/run/tests/run_refusals.rs` in scope and does not set `tests.modify`. Without that authorization the old assertion cannot be updated, which forces the deviation above.
+- The scope does not name `Cargo.lock`, although adding the runner and harness crates necessarily rewrites `osq-feature-run`'s entry there.
+
+Touched: Cargo.lock, crates/features/run/Cargo.toml, crates/features/run/src/feature.rs, crates/features/run/src/feature/dead.rs, crates/features/run/src/feature/done.rs, crates/features/run/src/feature/events.rs, crates/features/run/src/feature/markers.rs, crates/features/run/src/feature/refusals.rs, crates/features/run/src/feature/run.rs, crates/features/run/src/feature/scope.rs, crates/features/run/src/feature/start.rs, crates/features/run/src/feature/text.rs, crates/features/run/src/feature/verdict.rs, crates/features/run/tests/fixtures/fake-pi/run.sh, crates/features/run/tests/run_outcomes.rs
